    "type": "question",
    "label": "25",
    "prompt": "Find the values of $n$ for which the terms of the sequence $-86, -83, -80, \\ldots$ are positive.",
    "layout": "list",
    "columns": null,
    "questionDiagrams": [],
    "children": [],
    "answer": {
      "short": "$n=30,31,32,\\ldots$",
      "worked": "$a=-86$, $d=3$. For positive terms, $a_n>0$.\n$$\\begin{align*}-86+(n-1)3&>0\\\\-86+3n-3&>0\\\\3n&>89\\\\n&>\\frac{89}{3}\\end{align*}$$\nSince $n$ is a positive integer, $n=30,31,32,\\ldots$.",
      "solutionDiagrams": []
